<<<
calligraphy &c. should not be altered to calig-. Greek compounds

+ are made either with saAxu- from xadAos beauty, or with x«xado- from xadés beautiful. Choice is therefore between calligraphy & calography; & as the actual Greek compounds were xadduypagia &c., calligraphy is obviously right.
===
**calligraphy** &c. should not be altered to *calig-*. Greek compounds
+ are made either with καλλι- from κάλλος beauty, or with καλο- from καλός beautiful. Choice is therefore between *calligraphy* & *calography*; & as the actual Greek compounds were καλλιγραφία &c., *calligraphy* is obviously right.
>>>

<<<
callus. Pl. -uses; see -us. The word is often wrongly spelt callous, from confusion with the adjective.
===
**callus.** Pl. *-uses*; see ^^-US^^. The word is often wrongly spelt *callous*, from confusion with the adjective.
>>>

<<<
calmative, being queer both in pronunciation (k&’lmativ, not kah’mativ) & in formation (there is no Latin word for -ative to be attached to), should be left to the doctors, if even they have a use for it beside sedative, as a technical term.
===
**calmative**, being queer both in pronunciation (kă'lm*atĭv*, not kah'm*atĭv*) & in formation (there is no Latin word for *-ative* to be attached to), should be left to the doctors, if even they have a use for it beside *sedative*, as a technical term.
>>>

